{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ARw9kbUnPhiX1RgbReK7Vs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"1D seismic site response uniform layer transfer function cosine Kramer 1996 analytical closed form DOI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Analytical 1D transfer functions for layered soils - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0267726122003773\"},{\"title\":\"Theory and Examples — TransferFunctionTool 1.0.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://nheri-simcenter.github.io/TFT-Documentation/theory.html\"},{\"title\":\"Analytical 1D transfer functions for layered soils\",\"url\":\"https://authors.library.caltech.edu/records/vxn08-99g89\"},{\"title\":\"An accessible approach for the site response analysis of quasi-horizontal layered deposits | Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10518-018-0488-4\"},{\"title\":\"Seismic response analysis of soil profile: comparison of 1D versus 2D models and parametric study | Modeling Earth Systems and Environment\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40808-020-00737-6\"},{\"title\":\"PACIFIC EARTHQUAKE ENGINEERING RESEARCH CENTER Technical Manual for Strata\",\"url\":\"https://peer.berkeley.edu/sites/default/files/web_peer810_albert_r._kottke_ellen_m._rathje.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Analytical solution to the seismic response of visco-elastic soil layers\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/245410667_Analytical_solution_to_the_seismic_response_of_visco-elastic_soil_layers\"},{\"title\":\"A one-Dimensional Model for the Analysis of Seismic Site Response and Soil Instabilities: Review of the Computer Code SCOSSA 1.0[v1] | Preprints.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202510.1760\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) 1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/16861773/1D_harmonic_response_of_layered_inhomogeneous_soil_Analytical_investigation\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Soil-structure interaction: A state-of-the-art review of modeling techniques and studies on seismic response of building structures\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/built-environment/articles/10.3389/fbuil.2023.1120351/full\"}]\n\nThe search results provide information about 1D seismic site response transfer functions and reference Kramer's 1996 work. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nTransfer functions for layered soils have a mathematical structure defined as a superposition of independent harmonics, whose number, amplitudes and periods are fully characterized in closed-form in terms of layer properties.\n\nS. L. Kramer's work \"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\" was published by Pearson in 1996, and it appears to be a foundational reference for analytical approaches to 1D site response analysis.\n\nTransfer functions are used in both Seismology and Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering to relate seismic ground motion at different depths within strata.\n\nFor uniform layers specifically, wave amplitudes in a single uniform layer can be computed from boundary conditions, and for layered systems, wave amplitudes are calculated using recursive formulas developed by maintaining compatibility of displacement and shear stress at layer boundaries.\n\nA recent publication (2022) on the ScienceDirect platform appears to provide general closed-form expressions for customary transfer functions in 1D layered sites for any number of layers, expressed as sums of independent harmonics. However, the search results did not return a specific DOI number for the Kramer 1996 analytical closed-form solution you're seeking. The 2022 ScienceDirect article (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0267726122003773) may contain the specific DOI and mathematical formulations you're looking for.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dbc7cde-e70a-4bb0-94b0-45fd1a651a76","uuid":"18593591-16fa-484f-92e3-e8db80fe9f8d","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:36:58.280Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"1D seismic site response uniform layer transfer function cosine Kramer 1996 analytical closed form DOI","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HTQ8yb3Hn1hsWztXAPh9Jk","content":[{"title":"Analytical 1D transfer functions for layered soils - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0267726122003773"},{"title":"Theory and Examples — TransferFunctionTool 1.0.0 documentation","url":"https://nheri-simcenter.github.io/TFT-Documentation/theory.html"},{"title":"Analytical 1D transfer functions for layered soils","url":"https://authors.library.caltech.edu/records/vxn08-99g89"},{"title":"An accessible approach for the site response analysis of quasi-horizontal layered deposits | Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10518-018-0488-4"},{"title":"Seismic response analysis of soil profile: comparison of 1D versus 2D models and parametric study | Modeling Earth Systems and Environment","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40808-020-00737-6"},{"title":"PACIFIC EARTHQUAKE ENGINEERING RESEARCH CENTER Technical Manual for Strata","url":"https://peer.berkeley.edu/sites/default/files/web_peer810_albert_r._kottke_ellen_m._rathje.pdf"},{"title":"(PDF) Analytical solution to the seismic response of visco-elastic soil layers","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/245410667_Analytical_solution_to_the_seismic_response_of_visco-elastic_soil_layers"},{"title":"A one-Dimensional Model for the Analysis of Seismic Site Response and Soil Instabilities: Review of the Computer Code SCOSSA 1.0[v1] | Preprints.org","url":"https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202510.1760"},{"title":"(PDF) 1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation","url":"https://www.academia.edu/16861773/1D_harmonic_response_of_layered_inhomogeneous_soil_Analytical_investigation"},{"title":"Frontiers | Soil-structure interaction: A state-of-the-art review of modeling techniques and studies on seismic response of building structures","url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/built-environment/articles/10.3389/fbuil.2023.1120351/full"}]},"The search results provide information about 1D seismic site response transfer functions and reference Kramer's 1996 work. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nTransfer functions for layered soils have a mathematical structure defined as a superposition of independent harmonics, whose number, amplitudes and periods are fully characterized in closed-form in terms of layer properties.\n\nS. L. Kramer's work \"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\" was published by Pearson in 1996, and it appears to be a foundational reference for analytical approaches to 1D site response analysis.\n\nTransfer functions are used in both Seismology and Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering to relate seismic ground motion at different depths within strata.\n\nFor uniform layers specifically, wave amplitudes in a single uniform layer can be computed from boundary conditions, and for layered systems, wave amplitudes are calculated using recursive formulas developed by maintaining compatibility of displacement and shear stress at layer boundaries.\n\nA recent publication (2022) on the ScienceDirect platform appears to provide general closed-form expressions for customary transfer functions in 1D layered sites for any number of layers, expressed as sums of independent harmonics. However, the search results did not return a specific DOI number for the Kramer 1996 analytical closed-form solution you're seeking. The 2022 ScienceDirect article (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0267726122003773) may contain the specific DOI and mathematical formulations you're looking for."],"durationSeconds":7.731458333000017}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K2wqWxzot2J48MajthYbsw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Dobry Oweis Urzua 1976 simplified procedures fundamental period soil profile DOI BSSA\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Simplified procedures for estimating the fundamental period of a soil profile | Bulletin of the Seismological Society of America | GeoScienceWorld\",\"url\":\"https://pubs.geoscienceworld.org/ssa/bssa/article-pdf/66/4/1293/2700040/BSSA0660041293.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Simplified methods in Soil Dynamics | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/261292614_Simplified_methods_in_Soil_Dynamics\"},{\"title\":\"An Alternative Method to Estimate Fundamental Period of Layered Soil Deposit | Indian Geotechnical Journal | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40098-014-0121-7\"},{\"title\":\"Q'ACULATION OF PERIOD OF PROFILE IN FIGURE 1 1 BY METHOD 6 {SuccEsSIVE... | Download Table\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/QACULATION-OF-PERIOD-OF-PROFILE-IN-FIGURE-1-1-BY-METHOD-6-SuccEsSIVE-USE-OF-TwO-LAYER_tbl1_265747745\"},{\"title\":\"Importance of quantification of local site effects based on wave propagation in seismic microzonation | Journal of Earth System Science | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12040-008-0067-1\"},{\"title\":\"SIMPLIFIED METHODS IN SOIL DYNAMICS\",\"url\":\"https://studylib.net/doc/6630506/simplified-methods-in-soil-dynamics\"},{\"title\":\"Site classification of Turkish national strong-motion stations - Journal of Seismology\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10950-009-9182-y?error=cookies_not_supported&code=3742f03f-fac9-4b0f-aef7-c8bd692d6438\"},{\"title\":\"A New Approach for Calculating the Fundamental Period of Three-Layer Soil Deposits | Geotechnical and Geological Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10706-024-03015-9\"},{\"title\":\"Estimation of soil displacement profile for seismic design of underground structures in shallow soil | Bulletin of Engineering Geology and the Environment\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10064-024-03671-4\"},{\"title\":\"Application of Microtremor Horizontal-to-Vertical Spectral Ratio (MHVSR) Analysis for Site Characterization: State of the Art | Surveys in Geophysics\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10712-018-9464-4?error=cookies_not_supported&code=d18941eb-933b-480a-8c03-1b5a5779e74d\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the publication you're looking for:\n\n**Dobry, Ricardo, Issa Oweis, and Alfredo Urzua. \"Simplified procedures for estimating the fundamental period of a soil profile.\" Bulletin of the Seismological Society of America 1976; 66 (4): 1293–1321.**\n\n**DOI:** https://doi.org/10.1785/BSSA0660041293\n\n**Summary:**\nA study was made of simplified procedures for estimating the fundamental period, T, of a linear or equivalent linear model of a soil profile. Closed form solutions and approximate methods for computing the first period of an elastic shear-beam representation of the profile were examined.\n\nClosed form solutions are presented in chart form for the following cases: (a) shear-wave velocity increasing as a power of depth, (b) shear modulus increasing or decreasing linearly with depth, (c) two-layer profile, and (d) overconsolidated or uniform crust on layer with modulus increasing with depth. Methods 6 (Successive Use of Two-Layer Solution) and 7 (Simplified Version of the Rayleigh Procedure) gave errors less than 10 per cent for the period in all cases considered, and these methods are recommended for practical use.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dbc7cde-e70a-4bb0-94b0-45fd1a651a76","uuid":"930a0456-c735-4359-8a0c-e93d03e216b8","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:36:58.405Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Dobry Oweis Urzua 1976 simplified procedures fundamental period soil profile DOI BSSA","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DXFqy58hi9g2N9Vq7bQ25u","content":[{"title":"Simplified procedures for estimating the fundamental period of a soil profile | Bulletin of the Seismological Society of America | GeoScienceWorld","url":"https://pubs.geoscienceworld.org/ssa/bssa/article-pdf/66/4/1293/2700040/BSSA0660041293.pdf"},{"title":"Simplified methods in Soil Dynamics | Request PDF","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/261292614_Simplified_methods_in_Soil_Dynamics"},{"title":"An Alternative Method to Estimate Fundamental Period of Layered Soil Deposit | Indian Geotechnical Journal | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40098-014-0121-7"},{"title":"Q'ACULATION OF PERIOD OF PROFILE IN FIGURE 1 1 BY METHOD 6 {SuccEsSIVE... | Download Table","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/QACULATION-OF-PERIOD-OF-PROFILE-IN-FIGURE-1-1-BY-METHOD-6-SuccEsSIVE-USE-OF-TwO-LAYER_tbl1_265747745"},{"title":"Importance of quantification of local site effects based on wave propagation in seismic microzonation | Journal of Earth System Science | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12040-008-0067-1"},{"title":"SIMPLIFIED METHODS IN SOIL DYNAMICS","url":"https://studylib.net/doc/6630506/simplified-methods-in-soil-dynamics"},{"title":"Site classification of Turkish national strong-motion stations - Journal of Seismology","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10950-009-9182-y?error=cookies_not_supported&code=3742f03f-fac9-4b0f-aef7-c8bd692d6438"},{"title":"A New Approach for Calculating the Fundamental Period of Three-Layer Soil Deposits | Geotechnical and Geological Engineering","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10706-024-03015-9"},{"title":"Estimation of soil displacement profile for seismic design of underground structures in shallow soil | Bulletin of Engineering Geology and the Environment","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10064-024-03671-4"},{"title":"Application of Microtremor Horizontal-to-Vertical Spectral Ratio (MHVSR) Analysis for Site Characterization: State of the Art | Surveys in Geophysics","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10712-018-9464-4?error=cookies_not_supported&code=d18941eb-933b-480a-8c03-1b5a5779e74d"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the publication you're looking for:\n\n**Dobry, Ricardo, Issa Oweis, and Alfredo Urzua. \"Simplified procedures for estimating the fundamental period of a soil profile.\" Bulletin of the Seismological Society of America 1976; 66 (4): 1293–1321.**\n\n**DOI:** https://doi.org/10.1785/BSSA0660041293\n\n**Summary:**\nA study was made of simplified procedures for estimating the fundamental period, T, of a linear or equivalent linear model of a soil profile. Closed form solutions and approximate methods for computing the first period of an elastic shear-beam representation of the profile were examined.\n\nClosed form solutions are presented in chart form for the following cases: (a) shear-wave velocity increasing as a power of depth, (b) shear modulus increasing or decreasing linearly with depth, (c) two-layer profile, and (d) overconsolidated or uniform crust on layer with modulus increasing with depth. Methods 6 (Successive Use of Two-Layer Solution) and 7 (Simplified Version of the Rayleigh Procedure) gave errors less than 10 per cent for the period in all cases considered, and these methods are recommended for practical use."],"durationSeconds":6.914952250000031}}
