{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013EiDeZaNhGmZyB4iZYQUwz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Towhata 2008 \"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\" site response Bessel function power law shear modulus analytical solution\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering (Springer Series in Geomechanics and Geoengineering): Towhata, Ikuo: 9783540357827: Amazon.com: Books\",\"url\":\"https://www.amazon.com/Geotechnical-Earthquake-Engineering-Geomechanics-Geoengineering/dp/3540357823\"},{\"title\":\"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering (Springer Series in Geomechanics and Geoengineering) 2008, Towhata, Ikuo - Amazon.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.amazon.com/Geotechnical-Earthquake-Engineering-Geomechanics-Geoengineering-ebook/dp/B007HHKROI\"},{\"title\":\"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783540357827\"},{\"title\":\"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/298035737_Geotechnical_Earthquake_Engineering\"},{\"title\":\"Towhata, I. (2008) Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering. Springer Science & Business Media, Berlin. - References - Scientific Research Publishing\",\"url\":\"https://www.scirp.org/(S(i43dyn45teexjx455qlt3d2q))/reference/ReferencesPapers.aspx?ReferenceID=1717302\"},{\"title\":\"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2008gee..book.....T/abstract\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) (Springer Series in Geomechanics and Geoengineering) Ikuo Towhata Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering Springer (2008)\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/33172892/_Springer_Series_in_Geomechanics_and_Geoengineering_Ikuo_Towhata_Geotechnical_Earthquake_Engineering_Springer_2008_\"},{\"title\":\"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering - Ikuo Towhata - Google Books\",\"url\":\"https://books.google.com/books/about/Geotechnical_Earthquake_Engineering.html?id=wRxhiHf-ieIC\"},{\"title\":\"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering by Ikuo Towhata | Waterstones\",\"url\":\"https://www.waterstones.com/book/geotechnical-earthquake-engineering/ikuo-towhata/9783540357827\"},{\"title\":\"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering: Damage Mechanism Observed | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-3-642-36197-5_2-1\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for the query about Towhata 2008's \"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\" with focus on site response, Bessel functions, power law shear modulus, and analytical solutions.\n\nThe search results confirm that Towhata published \"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\" in 2008 with Springer Science & Business Media in Berlin. One research result notably mentions that \"Complete analytical solutions were developed for horizontal and vertical seismic accelerations considering wave velocities varying with depth as a generalized power-law function\" (Towhata, 2008).\n\nHowever, the search results do not provide detailed information specifically about the use of Bessel functions in the analytical solutions or the specific mathematical treatment of power law shear modulus variations in site response analysis. The search results primarily show bibliographic information and general descriptions of the book's scope, which covers site response analysis and equivalent linear methods, but the specific technical details about Bessel functions and power law solutions are not fully elaborated in these results.\n\nTo get more detailed technical information about the specific mathematical formulations and Bessel function applications in Towhata's work, you may need to access the book directly or search for related academic papers that cite this specific methodology.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dbc7cde-e70a-4bb0-94b0-45fd1a651a76","uuid":"5e7f1c79-61e6-4693-966e-1f