{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013fap8XdRESpTJcySCY5xsJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Rovithis Mylonakis Parashakis 2011 1D harmonic response layered inhomogeneous soil analytical DOI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation - University of Bristol\",\"url\":\"https://research-information.bris.ac.uk/en/publications/1d-harmonic-response-of-layered-inhomogeneous-soil-analytical-inv/\"},{\"title\":\"1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S026772611100008X\"},{\"title\":\"1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/229395024_1D_harmonic_response_of_layered_inhomogeneous_soil_Analytical_investigation\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) 1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/16861773/1D_harmonic_response_of_layered_inhomogeneous_soil_Analytical_investigation\"},{\"title\":\"Seismic Response of Inhomogeneous Soil Deposits with Exponentially Varying Stiffness | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 148, No 11\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/(ASCE)GT.1943-5606.0002850\"},{\"title\":\"Dynamic stiffness and kinematic response of single piles in inhomogeneous soil | Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10518-013-9473-0\"},{\"title\":\"Mode-based equivalent multi-degree-of-freedom system for one-dimensional viscoelastic response analysis of layered soil deposit - Earthquake Engineering and Engineering Vibration\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11803-018-0428-y?error=cookies_not_supported&code=9318e0f9-e217-4aea-8165-cc8879921026\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Seismic Response of Inhomogeneous Soil Deposits with Exponentially Varying Stiffness\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/360208957_Seismic_Response_of_Inhomogeneous_Soil_Deposits_with_Exponentially_Varying_Stiffness\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Geometrical Optics applied to 1D Site Response of Inhomogeneous Soil Deposits\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/339338353_Geometrical_Optics_applied_to_1D_Site_Response_of_Inhomogeneous_Soil_Deposits\"},{\"title\":\"Winkler Stiffness Intensity for Flexible Walls Retaining Inhomogeneous Soil | Proceedings | Vol , No\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/9780784481479.049\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the paper you're looking for:\n\nThe DOI is https://doi.org/10.1016/j.soildyn.2011.01.007\n\n**Full Citation:**\nRovithis, E. N., Parashakis, H., & Mylonakis, G. E. (2011). 1D harmonic response of layered inhomogeneous soil: Analytical investigation. Soil Dynamics and Earthquake Engineering, 31(7), 879-890.\n\n**Summary:**\nThe seismic response of inhomogeneous soil deposits is explored analytically by means of one-dimensional viscoelastic wave propagation theory, comprising a continuously inhomogeneous stratum over a homogeneous layer of higher stiffness, with excitation defined in terms of vertically propagating harmonic S waves imposed at the base of the system. The problem is treated analytically leading to an exact solution of the Bessel type for the natural frequencies, mode shapes and base-to-surface response transfer function.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dbc7cde-e70a-4bb0-94b0-45fd1a651a76","uuid":"0c91f4c0-d87b-4f21-a5bc-8a274b760e76","timestamp":"2026-03-29T13:37:11.575Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Rovithis Mylonakis Parashakis 2011 1D harmonic response layered inhomogeneous soil analytical DOI","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvt